      "title": "Example",
      "text": "Default progress bar.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "With label",
      "text": "Add a `label` prop to show a visible percentage. For low\npercentages, consider adding a min-width to ensure the label's text is\nfully visible.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Screenreader only label",
      "text": "Add a `visuallyHidden` prop to hide the label visually.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Contextual alternatives",
      "text": "Progress bars use some of the same button and alert classes for\nconsistent styles.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Striped",
      "text": "Uses a gradient to create a striped effect.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Animated",
      "text": "Add `animated` prop to animate the stripes right to left.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Stacked",
      "text": "Nest `<ProgressBar />`s to stack them.",
      "format": "md"
    }
